INSPIRED DESIGN OF THESE TOOLS
==============================

SKT is a redesign whose design is inspired by Harness 2, ScienceBuddy, and
RecursiveMAS. Each was used for what it does best, and each was ported into
this distribution in full so the result is one installable Python package
(`pip install .`) with a single CLI (`skt`), one config layer, one auth
store, and one sandbox/policy model shared across all three capabilities.

The reason for combining them: no single upstream tool provided a secure
coding-agent core, a reproducible multi-framework ML experiment platform,
and a recursive multi-agent reasoning/training system at the same time.
Harness 2 supplied the agent runtime and its policy-first security model,
ScienceBuddy supplied the benchmark and distributed-training platform, and
RecursiveMAS supplied the recursive multi-agent reasoning loops and their
GRPO trainer. SKT merges them under one name while keeping every upstream
license, copyright, and attribution intact.

1. Harness 2 (Google) -- Apache License 2.0
   Upstream tree: harness2-main
   License text: LICENSE (root of this distribution)
   Ported into this distribution as: the `impro/` core runtime -- including
   `impro.core` (agent loop, hooks, sandbox, permissions, budgets, streaming,
   tool registry, state), `impro.cli`, `impro.substrate`, `impro.benchmarks`,
   `impro.adapter`, `impro.config`, `impro.preflight`, and `impro.install`.
   Why we used it:
   - policy-first agent security, "policy-only" by default, with OS-level
     enforcement strictly opt-in;
   - a lifecycle-hook runtime that wraps every tool execution
     (PreToolUse -> execute -> PostToolUse) plus approval, audit, and
     secret-redaction plumbing;
   - deterministic, testable multi-agent orchestration with token and
     rollout budgets, streaming tool-arg accumulation, and compaction;
   - a mature CLI/TUI and session management (rollouts, resume, fork).
   SKT keeps this Apache-2.0 core intact: the `Copyright 2026 Google LLC`
   source headers, the Apache-2.0 root LICENSE, and functional protocol keys
   (`harness`, `harness.py`) are preserved. Only user-facing product text is
   branded as SKT.

2. ScienceBuddy -- MIT License
   Copyright (c) 2026 XShuhan
   Upstream tree: ScienceBuddy-main
   License text: impro/buddy/LICENSE
   Ported into this distribution as: the entire `impro.buddy` package (all
   51 upstream modules under ScienceBuddy `src/`), the `impro buddy` /
   `impro-buddy` / `impro-buddy-experiment` CLI commands, `IMPRO_BUDDY_*`
   environment variables, run configs, and the `scripts/buddy_train.py`
   launcher.
   Why we used it:
   - reproducible benchmark runs over standard datasets (MMLU, GPQA,
     HellaSwag, Math500, AIME, LiveCodeBench, ...) with model-as-judge and
     pass@k scoring;
   - multi-backend serving (VLLM, SGLang, Megatron) with health checks and
     rollout control;
   - Ray-based distributed training with placement groups, autoscaling, and
     multi-node topology support;
   - structured run configs, run persistence, and auto-generated HTML
     reporting.
   The MIT license and the `impro-buddy` package/CLI name are preserved as
   published.

3. RecursiveMAS -- MIT License
   Upstream tree: RecursiveMAS-main
   License text: impro/mas/LICENSE
   Ported into this distribution as: the entire `impro.mas` package (all 29
   upstream Python modules under RecursiveMAS `inference/` and `train/`),
   the `impro mas` CLI (`infer`, `train-inner`, `train-outer`), the
   `MAS_*` / `HF_*` / `IMPRO_MAS_*` environment variables, the bundled
   `requirements.txt`, and the bundled MedQA evaluation dataset
   (`impro/mas/inference/dataset/medqa.json`).
   Why we used it:
   - recursive, multi-turn agent reasoning with inner (agent) and outer
     (meta-agent) loops and prompt-level recursion control;
   - a GRPO trainer for multi-agent systems (inner and outer policy
     updates) with per-node LLM clients;
   - built-in evaluation over a Hugging Face dataset (MedQA) using Hugging
     Face models (e.g. `google/gemma-3-4b-it`).
   Upstream Hugging Face dataset and model repository IDs
   (`RecursiveMAS/...`, `google/gemma-3-4b-it`) are functional references and
   are preserved unchanged.

ATTRIBUTION OF BUNDLED MODELS AND DATASETS
=========================================

This distribution uses, but does not bundle, the following models and
datasets from the Hugging Face Hub:

1. Dataset: RecursiveMAS/R1_0528_filtered
   Used by: impro/mas/inference, impro/mas/train
   This dataset is based on deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1-0528, which is licensed
   under the MIT License. The original dataset was obtained from
   https://huggingface.co/datasets/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1-0528.

2. Dataset: RecursiveMAS/math_dataset
   Used by: impro/mas/train (GRPO training tasks)

3. Dataset: openbmb/M-A-P-Open-Reasoning-Corpus-Math
   Used by: impro/mas/train (reasoning task pool)

4. Dataset: google/genesis-docstring-python
   Used by: impro/mas/train (code task pool)

5. Model: RecursiveMAS/gemma-3-4b-it-unsloth-bnb-4bit
   Based on google/gemma-3-4b-it (Google DeepMind), quantized to 4-bit with
   Unsloth. Used by: impro/mas/inference, impro/mas/train.

6. Model: RecursiveMAS/gemma-3-12b-it-unsloth-bnb-4bit
   Based on gemma-3-12b-it (Google DeepMind), quantized to 4-bit with
   Unsloth. Used by: impro/mas/train (GRPO training backbone).

Model weights are not included in this source distribution. The Hugging
Face command-line tool must be used to download them, and users must agree
to the model license on Hugging Face before downloading.
